            <div xml:id="d313">

                <pb facs="0672" n="634" xml:id="pg634"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Edward M. House Papers</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Colonel E. M. House
                        to the British Prime Minister</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Lloyd George</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Green Wood Gate, Ashdown Forrest</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">Withyham, Sussex</hi></placeName>.<date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1919-08-12">August 12,
                        1919</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Prime Minister</hi>: Thank you so much for
                    wanting me to lunch yesterday with Grey and Haldane. I am sorry that I was not
                    well enough to be there.</p>
                <p>I want to congratulate you upon getting Lord Grey’s consent to go to the United
                    States. His appointment will have a splendid influence, and add to what you have
                    already done to bring our two countries closer together.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>[File copy not signed]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
